# Canonical citation metadata. GitHub reads this file to render the
# "Cite this repository" button.
#
# Authorship note: the citable author is the human director (Randy Crespo), with
# Dandelion Engineering as the affiliation/organization. AI tools are not listed
# as formal authors under current citation norms (they cannot take responsibility
# for the work), so the AI collaboration is disclosed in `abstract` instead. This
# is deliberate and matches Dandelion Engineering's transparency standard.
#
# License scope is intentionally NOT declared here: this work is path-scoped
# (MIT for code, CC BY 4.0 for prose, CC BY-SA 4.0 for dataset-derived figures,
# and the dataset itself under its source license), and CFF treats multiple
# `license:` values as "either/or," which would misstate that split.
# `LICENSING.md` is the authoritative license-scope record.
#
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "EEG to LFP: a bounded first rung toward \"electrical fMRI\""
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Crespo
    given-names: Randy
    affiliation: Dandelion Engineering
abstract: >-
  A completed study asking whether scalp EEG carries a subject-transferable
  signature of medial-temporal-lobe working-memory load, validated against
  simultaneous intracranial recordings in an open dataset of nine subjects. A
  pre-declared ladder of model classes failed a pre-declared bar, and the
  exploratory coupling lead did not survive residualization; both outcomes are
  reported. This work was directed by Randy Crespo (Dandelion Engineering) and
  produced in collaboration with the AI research agents Claude (Anthropic) and
  Codex (OpenAI); the AI contribution is disclosed here per Dandelion
  Engineering's transparency standard.
version: "1.0.0"
url: "https://github.com/Dandelion-Engineering/EEG-to-LFP"
